    "durationMs": 162713,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and verified end-to-end. Here's what I built:\n\n**Structure**\n- `app/` — FastAPI app: `main.py` (routes), `schemas.py` (URL/code validation), `models.py` (SQLAlchemy 2.x `Link` model), `database.py` + `config.py` (engine from `DATABASE_URL`, no hard-coded credentials, plain `postgresql://` URLs routed to psycopg 3)\n- `alembic/` — migrations reading `DATABASE_URL` from the env, with `0001_create_links` (unique `code`, `clicks` counter)\n- `start.sh` — runs `alembic upgrade head`, then `exec uvicorn` in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`\n- `README.md` with startup instructions, pinned `requirements.txt`, and `tests/`\n\n**Requirement details handled**\n- Custom validators keep the submitted URL byte-for-byte unchanged (pydantic's `HttpUrl` would normalize it); URL must be absolute http/https with a host\n- Codes validated as 4–20 `[A-Za-z0-9_-]` everywhere, including path params (422); generated codes are 8 random chars with collision retry plus an `IntegrityError` race fallback\n- Duplicate custom code → 409, unknown code → 404, malformed JSON/invalid input → 422, all with an `error` field via exception handlers\n- Clicks increment via an atomic `UPDATE ... clicks + 1`, exactly once per redirect, committed before the 302\n\n**Verification** — 10 pytest tests pass; I also ran the real `sh start.sh` server twice: all endpoints returned exact expected JSON/headers, and clicks (2) plus all rows survived a full restart. I stopped the server and truncated the `links` table so the graded run starts clean."
  }
